From 2b922883694976aa80974749fae874e9c7a2dacf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 05:59:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] parakeet: chunked long-audio encoding
 (TRANSCRIBE_PARAKEET_CHUNK_S)

Full-attention checkpoints without a VAD head keep every attention score
tensor at T x (2T-1) per head, so GPU memory is quadratic in clip length
(110m Q8_0, native WebGPU: 212 MiB at 56 s, 558 at 2.1 min, 1276 at 4.4 min).

With TRANSCRIBE_PARAKEET_CHUNK_S=<s> a clip longer than chunk + 2 x halo
(TRANSCRIBE_PARAKEET_CHUNK_HALO_S, default 4) and longer than
TRANSCRIBE_PARAKEET_CHUNK_MIN_S is encoded in equal windows: mel computed and
normalized once over the whole clip, each window = its own frames plus halo
seconds of real audio either side, windows start on the subsampling grid, only
the window's own encoder frames are kept, and the stitched encoder output is
decoded once (decoder state runs through the cuts; nothing to merge in text).

GPU peak is then one window's: 192-193 MiB from 2 to 9 min (110m), 529-576 MiB
(0.6b Q4_0); encoder time is linear. Not bit-identical to single-shot: frames
near a cut see halo seconds of context instead of the whole clip.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
